<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Three Creek Lake and Tam McArthur Rim (north approach)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:256-4: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="44.160159" lon="-121.636767"><ele>1572.2</ele><name>Upper Three Creek Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM way 100326940); confidence: high; pdf_page: 258; book_elev_ft: 5120; quote: map 58: UPPER 3 CREEK SNO-PARK 5120'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.160240" lon="-121.638620"><ele>1576.0</ele><name>Three Creek Lake Trail leaves Road 16</name><desc>source: USFS trail 4084 THREE CREEKS LAKE XC, BMP 0.0 (on OSM NF 16 node 38583495, 5 m); confidence: high; pdf_page: 257; quote: From the sno-park ski a few yards south up Road 16 past the gate and turn right onto the Three Creek Lake Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.153620" lon="-121.636240"><ele>1667.7</ele><name>Warren's Loop junction</name><desc>source: USFS trail 4084 BMP 0.7 (end of its first segment); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 258; quote: At 0.7 mile, after a demanding short ascent, the trail meets Warren's Loop</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.140530" lon="-121.644280"><ele>1787.5</ele><name>Near Jefferson View Shelter</name><desc>source: point of USFS trail 4084 nearest the shelter; shelter marked at 44.14078,-121.64504 in CalTopo 69BR and 44.141,-121.6451 in K3NT (67 m off the trail); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 258; quote: then 1.3 miles later passes near the Jefferson View Shelter in a large clearcut</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.124590" lon="-121.627030"><ele>1891.6</ele><name>Trail rejoins Road 16</name><desc>source: end of USFS trail 4084 (BMP 3.8) = OSM NF 16 node 38299531 (6 m); K3NT marker 'Jeff View Trail' 44.125,-121.627; confidence: high; pdf_page: 259; quote: From where the Three Creek Trail rejoins Road 16 after 4 miles</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.117960" lon="-121.628580"><ele>1930.8</ele><name>Trapper Meadow (Three Creek Meadow)</name><desc>source: OSM NF 16 node 3489644050 at K3NT marker 'Meadow TH' (11 m); Park Meadow Trail #96A (the book's Snow Creek return) leaves the road here; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 258; book_elev_ft: 6300; quote: map 58: TRAPPER MDW (3 CK MDW) 6300'; Road 16 0.5 from the trail; first view of Tam McArthur Rim is from Trapper Meadows, 1.5 miles below the lake</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.112125" lon="-121.622126"><ele>1945.6</ele><name>Road 370 junction (to Dutchman Flat)</name><desc>source: OSM node 2825719304 where NF 370 (way 357558084) leaves NF 16; 0.59 mi by road from wp 6 (map 0.6), 0.86 mi to the lake (map 0.9); confidence: high; pdf_page: 258; quote: map 58: Road 16 0.6 past Trapper Mdw to the 370 junction (TO DUTCHMAN FLAT), then 0.9 to the lake</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.100970" lon="-121.621920"><ele>1987.2</ele><name>Three Creek Lake, Tam McArthur Rim trailhead</name><desc>source: USFS trail 4078 BMP 0.0 = OSM NF 16 node 2825719291 (3 m), north-east shore of the lake; confidence: high; pdf_page: 258; book_elev_ft: 6560; quote: map 58: THREE CREEK LAKE 6560'; The best route from the lake is along the moderate, tree-covered ridge immediately to the east</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.086800" lon="-121.626270"><ele>2223.4</ele><name>East end of the rim (7,300 ft)</name><desc>source: OSM Tam McArthur Rim Trail #4078 node 7047989408 where it tops out on the rim; TALRRSF reaches 7,295 ft here; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 259; book_elev_ft: 7300; quote: climbs to the east end of the rim (7,300 feet)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.093002" lon="-121.643682"><ele>2357.8</ele><name>West end of Tam McArthur Rim Trail (summer viewpoint)</name><desc>source: last node (2826133331) of OSM Tam McArthur Rim Trail #4078 way 278139719 = USFS 4078 EMP 2.2 end; the same point is the destination (wp 8) of the Dutchman Flat tour or-vielbig-2e:268-1; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 259; quote: From the rimcrest follow gentle, vast snowfields through scattered stands of alpine trees</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.089110" lon="-121.658520"><ele>2388.5</ele><name>Flat ridge at 7,800 ft NE of Broken Top</name><desc>source: point on CalTopo TALRRSF line 3.36 mi from the lake, middle of its flat 7,800-7,840 ft stretch (3.2-3.55 mi); confidence: low; pdf_page: 259; book_elev_ft: 7800; quote: At 7,800 feet, a flat ridge northeast of Broken Top offers the finest views ... From the lake it is about 3 miles to this viewpoint</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Three Creek Lake and Tam McArthur Rim (north approach)</name><desc>1. Upper Three Creek Sno-Park -&gt; Three Creek Lake Trail leaves Road 16: osm (high), 0.11 mi | 2. Three Creek Lake Trail leaves Road 16 -&gt; Warren's Loop junction: usfs-trail (high), 0.71 mi | 3. Warren's Loop junction -&gt; Near Jefferson View Shelter: usfs-trail (high), 1.44 mi | 4. Near Jefferson View Shelter -&gt; Trail rejoins Road 16: usfs-trail (high), 1.72 mi | 5. Trail rejoins Road 16 -&gt; Trapper Meadow (Three Creek Meadow): osm (high), 0.51 mi | 6. Trapper Meadow (Three Creek Meadow) -&gt; Road 370 junction (to Dutchman Flat): osm (high), 0.59 mi | 7. Road 370 junction (to Dutchman Flat) -&gt; Three Creek Lake, Tam McArthur Rim trailhead: osm (high), 0.86 mi | 8. Three Creek Lake, Tam McArthur Rim trailhead -&gt; East end of the rim (7,300 ft): osm (medium), 1.49 mi | 9. East end of the rim (7,300 ft) -&gt; West end of Tam McArthur Rim Trail (summer viewpoint): osm (medium), 1.16 mi | 10. West end of Tam McArthur Rim Trail (summer viewpoint) -&gt; Flat ridge at 7,800 ft NE of Broken Top: osm (low), 0.88 mi</desc>
